What interests me most is what Alpöge says Claude contributed. He describes choosing the analogy that guided the attack. A known proof in a related setting gains leverage from repeated vanishing. Claude suggested how many operations called theta lifts to chain together to reproduce that effect over the integers. Alpöge acknowledges that some of the mathematics that followed outran his own understanding. The four-page note gives enough detail to see the idea and too little to judge whether the estimates work. 

If the independent checker accepts the entire proof against those standard statements, I’d regard RH as proved with very high confidence, even if a readable explanation takes much longer. And if Alpöge’s account of the discovery holds up, the bigger AI story is that an expert picked the right problem and analogy, and the model supplied a mathematical idea the expert himself hadn’t seen.

